  "hardware": {
    "family": "NVIDIA DGX Spark / GB10",
    "testedMachine": "One DGX Spark with 128 GB unified memory",
    "notes": [
      "Measured on one GB10, 2026-11-09, temperature 0: single-request decode 71 tok/s on code and 70 with thinking on (max mode 75.5 / 71.8); aggregate 93 tok/s at 8 requests and 180 at 64; cold TTFT 4.9 s at 8K and 20.9 s at 28K; every output byte-identical to serial decode at C1-C64.",
      "SparkQwen 0.7.0 on one GB10, 2026-11-10, RigMark protocol 1.1.0 (low reasoning effort, temperature 0), default mode: code 65.6, prose 29.3 and structured 85.2 tok/s decode estimates, cold 16K prefill 1,573 tok/s, 108 tok/s aggregate at 8 capped streams; 9 of 9 basic gates in the second of two rounds and 8 of 9 in the first, where one code answer ran to the token cap. The max mode read 75 to 79 on code and 120 on structured. With the loop guards off, a greedy answer that does not stop runs to the request's max_tokens. An identical prompt sent twice is prefilled again in full; a turn that extends a conversation hits the cache.",
      "Peak host memory: default about 111 GB, saver about 77 GB, max about 111 GB. The container is capped at 114 GiB because a GB10 that runs out of shared memory hangs instead of killing a process. In the default and max modes nothing else should use this Spark's GPU memory.",
      "The engine serves 127.0.0.1:8893 (fixed by the image) with host networking.",
      "Licenses: the Atlas engine in the image is AGPL-3.0-only (not included in LLooM). nvidia/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4, both drafters and TandemLLM's NVFP4 weights are Apache-2.0; TandemLLM's LICENSE and README are kept beside the weights for attribution."
    ]
  },
